// Canonical node types
//
// ErrorNode is THE canonical error node, shared by every package that records,
// clusters, validates, or mints from errors (KNIRVGRAPH's drq/nrv, KNIRVCHAIN's
// types, KNIRVARENA). It exists to end the divergence that previously left three
// incompatible Go structs and three overlapping proto messages
// (chain/v1.ErrorNode, lora/v1.ErrorContext, graph/v1.ErrorContext) describing
// the same thing — both of which were removed when this definition landed.
//
// Relationship to ErrorContext above: ErrorContext is the inbound *rich payload*
// an agent submits when it hits an error. ErrorNode is what the graph persists
// from that payload and what flows onward through clustering, validation and
// uLoRA minting. Nodes are created from a context, not equal to one.
//
// Everything DRQ needs is carried on the node itself: identity, classification,
// provenance, the Clustering group (cluster_id, embedding, priority,
// queue_position), payload, lifecycle, resolution, Red Queen dynamics and
// timestamps. A consumer can therefore reproduce or extend DRQ's clustering,
// scheduling and evolutionary state without reaching back into the graph.
